// HumanityOS home design: the ROW HOUSE FOR FRIENDS SHARING (2026-11-13, docs/design/home-room-program.md
// section 10), one home of a terrace on Row Street (data/blueprints/ship_structure.ron). A draft for
// developers (data/homes/starts.ron, `dev: true`).
//
// Five friends sharing (the operator, 2026-11-13: "Like maybe a group of friends pick a house to
// share"): five single bedrooms around one kitchen and one living room. Each single meets the space
// standard, 7.5 m2 and 2.15 m wide (the shared-house licensing rule asks 6.51 m2, SI 2018/616). Five
// sharing need a bathroom and a separate WC with a basin (SI 2006/373, Schedule 3: "one separate toilet
// with wash hand basin with appropriate splash back for every five sharing occupiers" and a bathroom).
// The standard has no row for five bedrooms and five people; the nearest are 97 m2 (4b5p) and 110 m2
// (5b6p) on two storeys. Plot 6.5 x 18 m; house 6.5 x 12 m, 156 m2 gross; yard 6.5 x 4 m = 26 m2.
// Ground: hall and stair, the step-free single 4.5 x 4.5 m at the front, the WC 2 x 2 m, a utility
// 2 x 2 m, kitchen and dining 4.5 x 4.5 m, the living room 3 x 4.5 m and a 2 x 2 m bay, on the yard.
// Upper: two singles at the front over the step-free one, and off a corridor across the back the
// bathroom, a second shower room and two singles 3.5 x 2.5 m, each with its window on the yard.
//
// Frame as the homesteads': the street is west, the door in the west wall, x the distance from the
// street, z along it. The side walls of the house are the party walls (the plot's shell); the
// gardens' edges are OPEN (`open_shell`): the yards behind a terrace are one green, each plot's
// north line marked by a mowing strip, the street edge a 0.9 m front garden wall with the gate.
// Every bedroom meets England's space standard inside its walls and every room is reached, lit and
// found by the game (crates/humanity-ship/src/home_program_tests.rs).
//
// Materials: 1 = steel (the shell), 2 = concrete, 3 = wood, 4 = glass, 9 = steel balustrade.
